column19:
This is pretty nice!  I&#x27;ve been doing the same for Verilog module declarations (which can easily have 100 arguments):<p><pre><code>    module fred(
        a,
        b,
        c
        );
    ...
    endmodule
</code></pre>
I&#x27;ve not tried it for function calls, but it&#x27;s not a bad idea...<p>How does it look for the case of an indented block after a while or a for? Let&#x27;s see:<p><pre><code>    while (
        a &&
        b && c
    ) {
        a = a + 1;
        b = b - 1;
    }
</code></pre>
Hmm, maybe better than what I do now...<p><pre><code>    while (a &&
           b && c) {
        a = a + 1;
        b = b - 1;
    }</code></pre>
